WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.535
-Our next guest can be seen
at the New York Comedy Cellar

00:00:03.535 --> 00:00:05.171
Tuesday, October 19th.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.840
Making his "Tonight Show" debut,

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.976
please welcome the very funny
Tom Thakkar.

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:11.210
♪♪

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.612
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:16.950
-Thank you. Hey. Oh, my gosh.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.952
Holy moly! Look at you!
Oh, my gosh!

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:21.187
This is incredible.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.755
It's so good to be here.

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:25.424
I've been aging rapidly!

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:29.729
I've been catching myself just
saying old-people stuff lately.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.598
I was walking down the street
the other day,

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:32.732
and I just heard myself go,

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:36.602
"That post office
used to be a bank!"

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:38.137
Who cares?

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:40.172
That's not a good story.
That sucks.

00:00:40.172 --> 00:00:41.707
That's an old-person story,
you know?

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:43.442
They're always telling you
stuff like that.

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:46.079
They're like, "That pizza place
was a spaghetti place before!"

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:48.581
"All right. Did you like
the spaghetti place?"

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.050
"No! It just was.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.553
You have to know what was."

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.421
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:57.223
I'm not -- I'm not that old yet.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:01:01.094
I'll know I'm really old when
I have a loud clock in my house.

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:03.730
Old people always have
the loudest clocks.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.197
You stay with an old person,

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:08.901
their clock is like,
"Bing, bong! Ding, dong!

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:12.272
Ding, dong! Bing, bong!

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.773
Bong!

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:15.141
Bong!

00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:16.609
Bong!

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:18.211
Bong!"

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.479
And then they're always like,

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.414
"I had trouble sleeping
last night."

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.149
You're like,
"Yeah, I wonder why."

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.484
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:27.553
[ Applause ]

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:29.488
Thank you.

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:32.358
I'm from Indiana.
I live in New York.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:35.228
But my family refuses
to visit me here and my friends,

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:36.996
because they're all scared
of New York.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.498
They think it's too dangerous,
which is crazy 'cause Indiana

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:42.201
is the most dangerous place
I've ever been.

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:44.537
When I was a kid,
our main form of entertainment

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.039
was a trampoline

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:48.975
that didn't have
the guard-net thing around it.

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:51.444
Those are like
little kid death traps.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.746
Every kid hobbles away like,
"Ugh.

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:56.916
We lost Jeremy back there.

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:59.752
And I'm different now."

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.421
My brother broke his leg
on our trampoline immediately

00:02:02.421 --> 00:02:03.956
'cause did he that thing
where he was like,

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:06.592
"I'm gonna go as high as I can
on the new trampoline,"

00:02:06.592 --> 00:02:08.360
and then he did,
and then he started

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:11.064
to float away
from the trampoline.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.832
You know that moment
where you see somebody

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:16.302
suspended in the air
and you're like, "Oh, no.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.404
We're about to hear
a new noise.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:19.705
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:21.574
That's going to be crazy."

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:24.577
But, uh, my brother broke
his leg, and then he made me --

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:27.079
We didn't want to tell my mom
what happened

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:28.748
'cause we didn't want
to lose the trampoline.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.716
So he made me drag him
into the house,

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:32.284
and then when my mom got home,

00:02:32.284 --> 00:02:34.921
we told her that my uncle
broke my brother's leg.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.622
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.622 --> 00:02:39.325
Because we were more willing
to lose him than a bouncy tarp,

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:42.395
so...

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:46.365
I got banned on Twitter
last year. This is true.

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:50.035
Because I got super into this
show called "My Cat From Hell."

00:02:50.035 --> 00:02:51.638
I don't know
if guys have seen it.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.005
It's the best show.
It's on Animal Planet.

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:54.874
It's like "The Dog Whisperer,"
but for cats.

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:57.743
And the host's name
is Jackson Galaxy,

00:02:57.743 --> 00:03:00.446
and he calls himself
"The Cat Daddy."

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:01.514
It's incredible.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.249
And I was watching it.
I was like, "Man.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.584
I bet this show has the best
Twitter account of all time

00:03:05.584 --> 00:03:07.753
with all these crazy cat people
and Jackson Galaxy."

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:10.523
I looked it up. They didn't
have a Twitter account!

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:13.659
But now they do.
Because I made one.

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:15.561
I made a Twitter account
for "My Cat From Hell."

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:18.564
And I got like 15,000 followers
because I played it straight.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:20.366
All I would tweet was like,
"Check out the show.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.468
Sundays at 9:00." You know?

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:26.839
"What was your favorite meowment
from tonight's episode?"

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.675
I did that for an entire year
like a psycho.

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:33.011
And it was so believable
that when people interviewed

00:03:33.011 --> 00:03:34.513
the host of the show,
they'd tag my Twitter account.

00:03:34.513 --> 00:03:36.950
They'd be like, "Follow him
here," and everybody did.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.484
And then a year in, I got drunk,

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.186
and I was like,
"Let's burn this thing down."

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.654
You know?

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:44.757
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:48.261
So, my first move
was I tweeted out,

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:50.263
"Hey, send in a picture
of your cat,

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:53.166
and I'll give it a rating
from 1 to 10."

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:55.367
And I got thousands
of cat pictures,

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:57.136
and I gave them all 3's.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.672
And people were so mad.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.808
I thought they might think
it was funny. They did not.

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:03.909
They were like,
"How dare you disrespect

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:05.678
my cat and my family."

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:08.147
And I was just like, "Hey, I'm
sorry your cat's a butter tail.

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:09.882
I don't know
what you want from me.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.785
I'm not attracted to your little
kitty cat, you pervert."

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:16.689
But I'd spell "pervert"
P-U-R-R-V-E-R-T.

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:18.925
Stay on brand.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:21.527
But what got me in trouble
was people were asking me

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:22.995
for cat advice all the time,

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:24.697
and I didn't know anything
about cats.

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.599
But I started giving advice.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.467
A lot of it was, like,
people going,

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:30.703
"Hey, my cat scratches our faces
every day."

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.438
And I was like,
"You've got to change

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:34.673
that cat's name, brother."

00:04:34.673 --> 00:04:36.643
The one that really got me
in trouble, though,

00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:39.045
is this guy goes, "Hey, my cat
keeps going to the bathroom

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:41.247
next to the litter box,
but he won't go inside.

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.882
Next to it.
I don't know what to do."

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.750
And I was like, "Look,
cats are very observant,

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.319
perceptive creatures.

00:04:47.319 --> 00:04:51.624
Sometimes they need to
see you go in the litter box

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:53.125
before they know what to do."

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:55.894
And right before I got banned,
I just saw one tweet

00:04:55.894 --> 00:04:59.431
from that dude that was like,
"This is not working."

00:04:59.431 --> 00:05:02.201
All right. I'm Tom Thakkar.
Thank you guys very much!

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:04.237
♪♪

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:06.172
-Hey!
That's how you do it, brother.

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:09.608
Oh, my gosh. Fantastic!
Tom Thakkar!

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:11.343
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:11.343 --> 00:05:14.079
He will be at
the New York Comedy Cellar

00:05:14.079 --> 00:05:16.049
Tuesday, October 19th.

